From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksandr Kulkov <adamant.pwn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:20:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix: rely on Chromium's PIN validation; cover
 collect-webauthn-pin in specs

Chromium's AuthTokenRequester already validates every entered PIN (length,
encoding, same as the current PIN) and asks again through CollectPIN() with
the error set, so Electron no longer validates it a second time with its own
rules. A callback from an earlier prompt in the same request is ignored, so
a late answer to a superseded prompt cannot answer the current one.

Specs on the simulated UV-locked security key cover a correct, wrong,
too-short and cancelled PIN. The no-listener warning now names the event
that enables PIN entry, and the docs describe `error` and `minPinLength`
as Chromium reports them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
